{
  "demonstrationId": "DEMO-8",
  "narration": {
    "narrationId": "NARRATION-8",
    "text": "This is a high value order so I checked it carefully. The invoice is 3051 per unit against 3000 agreed on the purchase order, which is a difference of 51 per unit, or 1.7 percent. That is inside the 2 percent maximum price variance, so on percentage alone I would release it. But there are 100 units, so the total overcharge is 5100, and the maximum absolute difference rule caps that at 5000. On a large order a small percentage is still a lot of money, which is exactly what that second rule is there to catch. Quantity is fine, 100 invoiced and 100 received, so this is purely a price issue and procurement need to review it."
  },
